"I wrote the Claude-faithful proposal: 2,027 lines covering all 14 sections, seven ASCII wireframes and three appendices mapping every audit defect, backlog item and open question to a phase.\n\n1. **Thesis:** the conversation is where things are made and the artifact is what you keep. Every made thing gets one id, is owned by the account, and follows one path: a card in the reply, a panel beside the chat, a full window at `/a/{id}`, then one link that also opens on the phone.\n2. **Design becomes a type, not a place.** The sidebar keeps one Artifacts row; the Design row goes on the web and never ships on the Mac glass branch. `/design` redirects to Artifacts filtered to designs. New designs come from asking, from **Make \u25b8 Design** in the composer (Claude's Output picker), or from **New \u25b8 Design** in Artifacts.\n3. **The data change comes first,** because DESIGN is already an artifact row. `Artifact` gains an owner (`userId`), and its conversation becomes an optional \"made in\" link. It also gains a project and a 30-day trash. A mutable working copy replaces folding design edits into old versions. Versions record their author, the message that made them, and whether they are complete, and a share link pins a specific version. New tables hold comments, access grants and exported files.\n4. **Work deliverables are split by shape.** Documents, reports and presentations become Doc and Deck artifacts, with the spec kept as the editable source and Office files as exports of a version. Spreadsheets, PDFs, archives and site zips stay in `WorkArtifact` and are listed by reference under Files. The schema comment at `schema.prisma:2613` explains why the table was separate; that reasoning holds for binaries but not for documents.\n5. **Native tolerance ships before any contract change.** One unknown kind blanks the Mac and iPhone library. One unknown sync entity stops sync for the whole account (`NativeSyncAPIClient.swift:141-190`). A small 1.6.x release cut from `main` must go out first, because the glass branch ships only when all its phases are done. The server then down-converts new kinds for older clients, keyed on a client-version header.\n6. **The X-01 preview fix ships with governance, not before it.** Previews move to a separate domain with `connect-src 'self'`. The same release adds ban propagation, admin takedown, a Report link, screening and rate limits. Public share pages move last.\n7. **One AI channel that reads the current version.** Follow-ups become targeted patches or design operations checked against the version the turn read, and people's edits win. Changes appear as edit cards in the transcript, and Ask Juno folds into the conversation. The stored transcript references artifact versions instead of copying their bodies, which removes the cause of X-05.\n8. **One view component keyed by artifact id** in six sizes. The version is data, never a React key or SwiftUI identity; that is the root fix for X-02, X-11 and X-12. Designs show server-rendered pictures everywhere and never JSON.\n9. **Where Juno beats Claude:**\n   - every type ships with versions, restore and trash on day one;\n   - every type has a comment-only role;\n   - publishing is separate from sharing and pinned to a version;\n   - the phone can view, play, comment, ask, make small edits and manage sharing, not just view.\n10. **Phases, in Claude's order:**\n\n    | Phase | Scope |\n    |---|---|\n    | 0 | Stop the bleeding |\n    | 1 | Artifacts become first-class objects |\n    | 2 | One surface; the owner starts dogfooding |\n    | 3 | Juno edits what is there; the owner's \"day one\" |\n    | 4 | Docs, Decks and Work; public launch, Design door removed |\n    | 5 | People: grants, comments, notifications |\n    | 6 | Design systems |\n\n11. **Guard rails:** everything sits behind reversible per-account flags. Redirects stay 307 until the public launch. Migrations are additive before any constraint flips. Section 13.3 lists 15 must-not-ship-before rules for release review.\n12. **Two claims to recheck:** the design library's version comparison and the phone contract lean on the glass branch's stage 3 work as described in its plan doc, and I have not run that branch.\n13. **Coordination:** merge and deploy `7243613f` now. Phase 2 starts only after the separate X-02 fix lands.\n14. **Twenty owner decisions are in \u00a714.2, each with a recommendation.** The main ones: the Work split above; Artifacts stays a sibling of Library; publishing is a pinned snapshot while grants give live access; regenerate never deletes; comments get their own table. Also: one network allowlist on web, Mac and iPhone; no artifacts in private chats for now; `/a/{id}` as the link; spreadsheets are not a type in v1; the tolerant release goes out from `main` now.\n15. **To do outside this session:** the Figma, GitHub, Notion, Slack, Linear and other plugin connectors need authorising in their connector settings before they work.\n\nFile: `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/merge/proposal-claude-faithful.md`"